From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Yuwei <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:43:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Make the line after a final break only where asked

`Layout::set_line_after_final_break`: whether the line after a forced break
that ends the text (a newline last) is made. By default it is, as before: an
editor puts the caret there.

CSS makes no line box after the last forced break when nothing follows it,
so `<div>a<br></div>` is one line tall. Not made, the line is taken back
once committed, before anything is yielded, so a caller breaking lines one
at a time never sees it either.
---
 parley/src/layout/data.rs            |  5 ++
 parley/src/layout/layout.rs          | 13 ++++
 parley/src/layout/line_break.rs      | 12 ++++
 parley/src/tests/mod.rs              |  1 +
 parley/src/tests/test_final_break.rs | 95 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 126 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 parley/src/tests/test_final_break.rs

